.DS_Store
.merlin
.env
.history
.vscode
npm-debug.log
**/lib
/node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.grapqhl_ppx_cache
coverage
lerna-debug.log
.playwright-mcp

# Compiled outputs under inline demo dirs inside rescript binding packages
# (rescript/*/src/example/ and rescript/*/src/examples/). These are usage
# demos, not deployables — their `.res.mjs` regenerates on every build and
# isn't part of the publish surface.
#
# Outputs under the top-level `examples/` (monorepo example apps) ARE tracked:
# they're the entry points for Pulumi deploys and `pnpm run run` scripts,
# and ReScript only emits in-source for build-root packages, so we can't
# rely on `pnpm run build` to regenerate them transitively.
rescript/*/src/example/**/*.res.mjs
rescript/*/src/examples/**/*.res.mjs

# Auto Claude data directory
.auto-claude/

# Auto Claude generated files
.auto-claude-security.json
.auto-claude-status
.claude_settings.json
.worktrees/
.security-key
logs/security/

# Reventless PPX dune build output
packages/reventless-ppx/src/_build/

# Native build artifacts (e.g. reventless-ppx per-platform binaries) are
# distributed via the npm registry as @reventlessdev/reventless-ppx-<target>
# packages, never committed. Local builds via `pnpm build:ppx` land alongside
# the launcher and serve only as a fallback for PPX hackers.
#
# Exception: packages/reventless-ppx/ppx-osx-x64.exe remains tracked as the
# macOS local-fallback until darwin-* per-platform packages publish. Tracked
# files are unaffected by this pattern (gitignore is for untracked files).
*.exe

# Lambda layer zip artifacts are built by reventless-layer-builder and
# uploaded directly by CI — never committed. The package-local gitignore at
# reventless/reventless-layer-builder/.gitignore covers the build output;
# this repo-wide rule catches strays from any future layer builders.
**/reventless-layer*.zip

# Local SQLite databases written by the in-memory platform's persistence mode
# (default path documented in docs/guides/local-persistence.md).
.reventless/

# ast-grep tree-sitter grammar (compiled binary, rebuild with gcc)
rescript.dylib

# This is a pnpm workspace — the root pnpm-lock.yaml is the only authoritative
# lock. Per-package npm package-lock.json files are stale npm-era leftovers that
# nothing consumes (a dependency's lockfile is never honored by consumers).
package-lock.json

# Per-dev Pulumi config overrides — gitignored sidecar layered on top of the
# checked-in `Pulumi.<stack>.yaml` files. Read by `Util_LocalConfig` at
# deploy time. Keep dev-local values (e.g. existing AWS resource IDs)
# off shared stack configs.
**/Pulumi.local.yaml

# Cross-repo dev linking (see docs/guides/cross-repo-dev-linking.md).
# pnpm-workspace.base.yaml is the tracked source of truth.
# pnpm-workspace.yaml is either a symlink to it (release mode) or a
# merged file produced by `pnpm link:on` (link mode) — always local.
# pnpm-workspace.local.yaml is the developer's overlay input.
pnpm-workspace.yaml
pnpm-workspace.local.yaml